\end{align*}

For the second inequality, \(-2y \leq 12\), we simplify it as follows:
\begin{align*}
-2y &\leq 12 \\
y &\geq -6
\end{align*}

For the third inequality, \(-4y \geq 2y+17\), simplifying it gives:
\begin{align*}
-4y &\geq 2y + 17 \\
-6y &\geq 17 \\
y &\leq -\frac{17}{6}
\end{align*}

The common solutions are those that satisfy all three inequalities simultaneously. From the simplified inequalities, the common solutions are \(y\) such that:
\begin{align*}
-6 &\leq y \leq -\frac{17}{6} \\
&\approx -6 \leq y \leq -2.83
\end{align*}

Since \(y\) must be an integer, the possible values of \(y\) are:
\begin{align*}
y &= -6, -5, -4, -3
\end{align*}

Thus, there are \(\boxed{4}\) common integer solutions to the three inequalities.

